Section B – SQL Practical Questions

1- Write an SQL query to create a database named CustomerDB.
2- Write an SQL query to select the CustomerDB database.
3- Write an SQL query to create a Customers table with the following columns: Customer_ID, Customer_Name, Email, Phone, City, and Age. Apply appropriate data types and constraints to the columns.
4- Write SQL queries to insert at least 5 records into the Customers table.
5- Write an SQL query to display all records from the Customers table.
6- Write an SQL query to display only the Customer_Name, Email, and City columns from the Customers table.
7- Write an SQL query to update the city of a customer using Customer_ID.
8- Write an SQL query to delete a customer using Customer_ID.
9- Write an SQL query to add a new column named Gender to the Customers table.
10- Write an SQL query to rename the Customer_Name column to Full_Name.
11- Write an SQL query to remove the Gender column from the Customers table.
12- Write an SQL query to remove all records from the Customers table while keeping the table structure.
13- Write an SQL query to permanently delete the Customers table.
14- Write an SQL query to create a Customers table where Customer_ID is the PRIMARY KEY.
15- Write an SQL query to create a Customers table where Email must contain UNIQUE values.
16- Write an SQL query to create a Customers table where Customer_Name cannot contain NULL values.
17- Write an SQL query to create a Customers table where Age must be greater than or equal to 18.
18- Write an SQL query to create a `Customers table where the default value of City is Mumbai.
